1
00:00:04,625 --> 00:00:08,700
The dark carton scores 0.94 for damage, the mailer
0.83.

2
00:00:09,371 --> 00:00:12,070
Both clear the priority threshold of 0.70.

3
00:00:13,095 --> 00:00:15,470
Both parcels are in frame and in focus.

4
00:00:16,090 --> 00:00:17,815
The minimum brightness is 0.20.

5
00:00:18,460 --> 00:00:21,885
The carton stops at 0.12, the mailer at 0.64.

6
00:00:22,555 --> 00:00:24,355
Which photo gets the inspection slot?

7
00:00:26,980 --> 00:00:28,130
Inspect the mailer.

8
00:00:28,800 --> 00:00:30,950
You can follow the split in its folded seam.

9
00:00:31,595 --> 00:00:34,570
For the dark carton, ask for a retake in better
light.

10
00:00:35,215 --> 00:00:37,365
Keep its original score with the request.

11
00:00:38,207 --> 00:00:40,956
Normal and priority photos go to a specialist.

12
00:00:41,602 --> 00:00:43,501
The specialist inspects the parcel.

13
00:00:44,325 --> 00:00:45,650
Back to the dark carton.

14
00:00:46,295 --> 00:00:49,670
Its brightness is 0.12, below the 0.20 minimum.

15
00:00:50,352 --> 00:00:52,877
A human also marked this image unusable.

16
00:00:53,877 --> 00:00:55,377
Keep those exact pixels.

17
00:00:56,047 --> 00:00:58,622
Change only the reported brightness to 0.30.

18
00:00:59,267 --> 00:01:02,517
The parcel is visible and the blur reading is within
the limit.

19
00:01:03,162 --> 00:01:04,812
What route does that change produce?

20
00:01:07,337 --> 00:01:09,037
Now it goes to priority review.

21
00:01:09,707 --> 00:01:12,357
The specialist would still open the same dark
picture.

22
00:01:13,002 --> 00:01:18,152
Comparing the route with the human label catches an
unusable photo in the priority queue.
